 The retired keys `how explorer`, `how explainer`, `why investigators`, and `why synthesizer` can remain in a saved file. Read, resolve, and budget leave them out of `config`, list them in `droppedRoles`, and do not validate their values. The next write omits them and lists them in its `droppedRoles`. Every other saved value stays unchanged.
 
+A role with any entry for the removed Pi executor (`"executor": "pi"`), as a scalar or anywhere in a list, can also remain in a saved file. Read, resolve, and budget leave the whole role out of `config` and do not validate its values. They list it in `retiredExecutorRoles` as `{ "role": "ROLE", "executor": "pi" }`. Resolve then treats it as unconfigured, so it yields native `inherit-parent` entries at the original cardinality with `source: "unconfigured"`. The next write omits it and returns the same `retiredExecutorRoles`. A submitted Pi entry fails with a message that Pi was removed, naming the role. Any other unknown executor still fails validation.
+
 Ordered lists preserve duplicate seats. Each role has a starting effort. `hardest tasks` starts at `max`. `reflect tooling`, `swarm workers`, the three panels, and the cross-judge pool start at `high`. The other roles start at `xhigh`. A budget moves every starting effort by steps on the ladder `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, `max`. `unlimited` raises it one step, `large` keeps it, `medium` lowers it one step, and `small` lowers it two steps. A target stays at either end of the ladder. A budget preview maps each saved exact entry to the highest effort its executor and model support at or below the role's target. Parent aliases retain the actual parent's settings.
 
 ## Commands
 
-- `read [--codex-home ABS]` returns `file`, `exists`, `sha256`, `config`, `targetReasoningEffort`, full unresolved `proposal`, `needsChoice`, and `droppedRoles`. Saved roles prefill the proposal. Read never writes.
-- `resolve --role "ROLE" [--codex-home ABS]` returns `role`, `entries`, `source`, `file`, `budget`, `targetReasoningEffort`, and `droppedRoles`. Its `targetReasoningEffort` is that role's target. Use one subagent per entry for panel roles. The judge pool remains a selection pool.
+- `read [--codex-home ABS]` returns `file`, `exists`, `sha256`, `config`, `targetReasoningEffort`, full unresolved `proposal`, `needsChoice`, `droppedRoles`, and `retiredExecutorRoles`. Saved roles prefill the proposal. Read never writes.
+- `resolve --role "ROLE" [--codex-home ABS]` returns `role`, `entries`, `source`, `file`, `budget`, `targetReasoningEffort`, `droppedRoles`, and `retiredExecutorRoles`. Its `targetReasoningEffort` is that role's target. Use one subagent per entry for panel roles. The judge pool remains a selection pool.
 - `catalog --input ABS [--claude-runtime ABS]` normalizes native Codex `model/list` results or combined confirmed model capabilities. Collect every native catalog page first. The optional runtime file is the Claude runner's `detect` receipt. It records an absolute executable, CLI version at least `2.1.280`, required print/model/effort/output-format/verbose/resume options, global `effortSyntax`, and `modelExecutionVerified: false`. It does not enumerate account models. Normalized catalogs retain the runtime under `runtimes` and model sources. Normalizing them again produces the same result.
-- `budget --budget unlimited|large|medium|small --catalog ABS [--codex-home ABS]` previews the sparse saved config while preserving role model choices, lists, and aliases. It also returns `droppedRoles`. `needsChoice` lists entries without a confirmed effort at or below their role's target, each with that `targetReasoningEffort`. This command never writes.
-- `write --input ABS --catalog ABS --expected-hash HASH|absent [--codex-home ABS] [--dry-run]` validates then saves an accepted config or a resolved `budget` result. Use the hash from the read that informed the confirmed choices. A stale hash, malformed preference, unconfirmed model, or unsupported effort prevents writing. Dry run validates the full proposal without creating a destination. `droppedRoles` lists the retired keys the write omits.
+- `budget --budget unlimited|large|medium|small --catalog ABS [--codex-home ABS]` previews the sparse saved config while preserving role model choices, lists, and aliases. It also returns `droppedRoles` and `retiredExecutorRoles`. `needsChoice` lists entries without a confirmed effort at or below their role's target, each with that `targetReasoningEffort`. This command never writes.
+- `write --input ABS --catalog ABS --expected-hash HASH|absent [--codex-home ABS] [--dry-run]` validates then saves an accepted config or a resolved `budget` result. Use the hash from the read that informed the confirmed choices. A stale hash, malformed preference, unconfirmed model, or unsupported effort prevents writing. Dry run validates the full proposal without creating a destination. `droppedRoles` lists the retired keys the write omits, and `retiredExecutorRoles` lists the retired-executor roles it omits.
 
 The top-level `targetReasoningEffort` of `read` and `budget` is the effort the budget label names, which is the target of a role that starts at `xhigh`. Per-role targets appear in proposal slots, `resolve`, and `needsChoice` entries.
 
